{"availability":"available","full":"GraphicMeat/mail-vault-app","name":"mail-vault-app","description":"Local private email backup","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":92,"forks":8,"created":"2026-02-11T12:50:29Z","updated":"2026-10-09T13:09:10Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mailvaultapp.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://mailvaultapp.com/demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:17.479Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:17.479Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:17.479Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:17.479Z","stars":92,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A local-first email client that files every message on your own disk as a plain .eml, so you can delete it from the server and still keep your copy.","MailVault is a full email client with a vault behind it. You read, search, thread and reply the way you would in any client, and every message you keep is written to your own disk as a standard .eml file in a Maildir tree, readable by anything. When the provider deletes it, expires it, or asks you to pay for storage, your copy does not care."],"features":["Your mail outlives the server. Every message you keep is a plain .eml on your own disk, and it stays there after the provider deletes it.","You can see what is safe. Each row shows whether a message is on the server, in the vault, in both, or only on your disk.","Clear the server without losing anything. Archive and delete in one step (Premium), or thousands at once by year, with crash-safe recovery. Archive, Back up & Delete (Premium) also copies each message to your backup…","Find anything, offline. SQLite FTS5 search over the whole vault: 50,000 messages searched in under 15 ms in our test.","No lock-in. Maildir and MBOX, readable by Thunderbird, Apple Mail or grep."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GraphicMeat/mail-vault-app/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dd17a7fa10979fceefdcb1665e8bdfae0e248ecde11ed5f33